<edge source="china_tech_pressure::external_countermeasures" target="global_finance_shock::sovereign_fiscal_pressur" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating external countermeasures (investment bans, sanctions, asset restrictions) trigger export losses and capital outflows in targeted economies, reducing tax revenues and prompting emergency spending and higher borrowing needs that raise sovereign fiscal pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_pressure::external_countermeasures" target="russia_ukraine_war::service_restriction_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased sanctions, designations and investment curbs by third states raise legal and financial risk for operators, prompting more frequent geofencing, throttling or suspension of services affecting actors in the conflict zone.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_pressure::external_countermeasures" target="us_iran_standoff::allied_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in third‑party countermeasures against China (sanctions, investment curbs, designations) prompts Beijing to signal or deepen strategic ties with Iran, which in turn leads the US and regional partners to align more closely politically and operationally to counter the perceived China‑Iran axis.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_pressure::external_countermeasures" target="us_iran_standoff::shipping_disruption_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened external countermeasures against China escalate US‑China strategic competition and drive reallocation of Western naval and intelligence assets toward the Indo‑Pacific, reducing deterrent presence in the Gulf and thereby increasing the risk of commercial shipping delays, reroutings, or incidents tied to the US‑Iran standoff.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
