<edge source="global_finance_shock::monetary_policy_stance" target="china_tech_pressure::corporate_repositioning" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A tightening monetary policy stance (higher real rates) raises borrowing and working‑capital costs and reduces cross‑border financing, which increases firms' incentives to relocate production closer to demand or to diversify suppliers to lower financing and inventory risks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shock::monetary_policy_stance" target="democratic_unrest_wave::investor_risk_aversion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid monetary tightening raises short-term rates and market volatility and depresses risky asset valuations, prompting investors to shift toward safe assets and increase measured risk aversion.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shock::monetary_policy_stance" target="russia_ukraine_war::provider_control_autonom" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A tighter monetary stance raises borrowing costs and liquidity stress for commercial satellite/communications firms, forcing them into government loans, conditional financing or creditor covenants that curtail their unilateral decision‑making over service allocations.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shock::monetary_policy_stance" target="us_iran_standoff::allied_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained tightening in global monetary policy raises borrowing costs and inflationary pressures for US partners, forcing domestic budget retrenchment and politically constraining willingness to absorb additional security burdens, which erodes coalition alignment in an Iran crisis.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
