<edge source="global_finance_shock::real_output_growth" target="china_tech_pressure::corporate_repositioning" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Falling real output growth reduces demand and raises country- and buyer-concentration risk, prompting firms to accelerate supply‑chain diversification, shorten production networks and reallocate market exposure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shock::real_output_growth" target="democratic_unrest_wave::protest_event_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher real output growth reduces unemployment and income loss; conversely, a marked downturn (falling growth) quickly increases joblessness and grievance-driven demonstrations, so increases in growth lower protest frequency.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
</edge>
