<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::protest_event_rate" target="china_tech_pressure::external_countermeasures" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising frequency of visible protest events that implicate foreign-made surveillance or communications technologies prompts other states and parliaments to impose sanctions, investment restrictions and designations against the suppliers of those technologies.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::protest_event_rate" target="global_finance_shock::real_output_growth" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained increase in protest frequency directly disrupts production, retail, transport and workforce availability (strikes, blockades, shop closures), causing measurable declines in quarterly GDP and industrial output.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::protest_event_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::state_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large or sustained protest waves increase the political salience of communications flows, motivating governments to escalate diplomatic, regulatory or financial pressure on commercial satellite providers to alter or restrict services perceived as facilitating opponents or foreign military use.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::protest_event_rate" target="us_iran_standoff::allied_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising domestic protests in U.S. partners force those governments to prioritize internal stability and constrain their political and military willingness to coordinate openly with Washington on Iran-related pressure campaigns, reducing coalition cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
