<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::policy_forcefulness" target="china_tech_pressure::tech_controls_tightness" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">When states respond to unrest with more forceful policing and legal crackdowns they simultaneously mandate expanded digital surveillance, mandatory data access and tighter platform compliance, directly increasing the tightness of technology controls.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::policy_forcefulness" target="global_finance_shock::sovereign_fiscal_pressur" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">More forceful state responses raise immediate security and enforcement expenditures and often require emergency transfers or revenue foregone while economic activity falls, widening budget deficits and near‑term refinancing needs.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::policy_forcefulness" target="russia_ukraine_war::service_restriction_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">States responding more forcefully to unrest rapidly deploy export controls, telecom directives and legal orders that require or enable commercial operators to throttle, block or refuse satellite service to designated zones or actors in the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::policy_forcefulness" target="us_iran_standoff::proxy_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.68</data>
  <data key="d36">Heavy-handed state repression increases regime calculation that asymmetric retaliation via allied proxies is an effective deterr (and gives proxies recruiting narratives), prompting more proxy strikes against perceived external supporters such as U.S. forces and partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
