<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::contagion_susceptibility" target="china_tech_pressure::state_policy_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater propensity for unrest to spread across borders incentivizes governments to ramp up directed economic and regulatory interventions (subsidies, procurement rules, licensing limits) to harden the domestic tech sector against external shocks, raising state policy intensity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::contagion_susceptibility" target="global_finance_shock::energy_supply_balance" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher susceptibility makes unrest more likely to spread to energy‑producing or transit nodes (pipelines, ports, fields), producing simultaneous regional outages that tighten supply relative to demand.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="democratic_unrest_wave::contagion_susceptibility" target="us_iran_standoff::military_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.62</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher propensity for unrest to spread across borders raises the likelihood that neighboring states and external patrons (including the U.S. and Iran) escalate military posturing and cross-border deployments to deter spillover and protect interests, increasing overall military tension.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">democratic_unrest_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
